## Category 1 — Missing Inner Functions (Not Assigned to Any Target File)

These functions exist inside [registerRoutes()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes.ts#325-6272) but are **not mentioned anywhere** in the implementation plan or task.md. Each needs a target file.

| # | Function | Lines | Purpose | Suggested Target File |
|---|----------|-------|---------|----------------------|
| 1 | [loadQuoteSnapshotConfig()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes.ts#4987-5001) | L4987–5000 | Reads `staleThresholdMs`, `fxRolloverTz`, `fxRolloverTime` from systemConfig | `server/routes/public/quotes.ts` or new `server/lib/quoteSnapshotUtils.ts` |
| 2 | [loadPrevCloseMap(symbols, sessionDay)](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes.ts#5002-5037) | L5002–5036 | Raw SQL query for `market_daily_close` previous closes with fallback | Same as above |
| 3 | [buildQuoteView(quote, prevCloseMap, nowMs, staleThresholdMs)](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes.ts#5038-5082) | L5038–5081 | Constructs enriched quote object (spread, pctChange, stale, marketOpen) | Same as above |
| 4 | [buildQuoteSnapshotResponse(symbols?)](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes.ts#5083-5179) | L5083–5178 | Full snapshot pipeline: hub → Valkey → per-key Valkey → Postgres fallback | Same as above |
| 5 | [normalizeSymbolsInputRaw(raw)](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes.ts#5180-5189) | L5182–5188 | Comma-split + trim + uppercase for REST query param parsing | Same as above |
| 6 | [getAllowedQuoteSymbolsForRequest(req)](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes.ts#5190-5195) | L5190–5194 | Resolves allowed symbols set for the current request's session user | Same as above |
| 7 | [loadLegalReacceptState(userId)](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes.ts#1686-1747) | L1686–1746 | Computes legal re-acceptance status (SHA256 comparison, blocked state) | `server/routes/auth/currentUser.ts` (inner helper) |
| 8 | [buildCurrentUserPayload(...)](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes.ts#1748-1788) | L1748–1787 | Builds the response object for GET /api/auth/current-user | `server/routes/auth/currentUser.ts` (inner helper) |
| 9 | [writeDecisionReject(rejectReason, riskLimit, riskObserved)](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes.ts#3248-3269) | L3249–3268 | Inner helper for audit writes during trade open rejections | `server/routes/trader/tradeOpen.ts` (inner helper) |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Items 1–6 are **the entire quote snapshot pipeline** (~200 lines). The plan mentions `quotes.ts` in `server/routes/public/` but doesn't enumerate these functions. They use raw SQL via `dbClient.query()` (not Drizzle ORM) which is a security audit point — the plan's checklist says "All DB queries use parameterized Drizzle ORM (no raw SQL string interpolation)" but [loadPrevCloseMap](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes.ts#5002-5037) uses parameterized raw SQL (`$1::text[]`), and [buildQuoteSnapshotResponse](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes.ts#5083-5179) has an inline raw SQL block at L5130–5168.

