## Category 4 — Missing Module-Level Constants & Mutable State

These are defined at the top of [registerRoutes()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes.ts#325-6272) or inside it, but are not enumerated in the plan's "Captured Binding" table:

### Constants (not in plan table)

| # | Constant | Line | Value |
|---|----------|------|-------|
| 12 | `EMAIL_VERIFICATION_GRACE_PERIOD_MS` | L202 | `14 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000` (14 days) |
| 13 | `VALID_MOODS` | L4732 | Array of 7 valid mood strings for journal entries |
| 14 | `wsMaxPayloadBytes` | L5301–5304 | Clamped from env `WS_MAX_MESSAGE_BYTES` |
| 15 | `wsTransportTlsRequired` | L5394–5399 | Computed from NODE_ENV + env vars |
| 16 | `wsOriginValidationEnabled` | L5400–5402 | Env toggle |
| 17 | `wsAllowMissingOrigin` | L5403–5407 | Env toggle |
| 18 | `wsUserConnectionLimit` | L5408–5411 | Clamped from env `WS_MAX_CONNECTIONS_PER_USER` |
| 19 | `wsMessageRateLimitPerWindow` | L5412–5415 | Clamped from env `WS_MESSAGE_RATE_LIMIT` |
| 20 | `wsMessageRateWindowMs` | L5416–5419 | Clamped from env `WS_MESSAGE_RATE_WINDOW_MS` |
| 21 | `wsAllowedOrigins` | L5420–5431 | `Set<string>` populated from env `WS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` + `APP_URL` |
| 22 | `wsPolicyRecheckMs` | L6079 | From env `WS_JURISDICTION_RECHECK_MS` (default 30s) |

> [!NOTE]
> The plan's `WsHelperDeps` interface at L227–239 captures some of these (items 16–21) but doesn't show where they are initialized or that they are env-parsed with clamping. The clamping logic needs to move with them — not just the values.

### Mutable State Variables (not enumerated individually)

| # | Variable | Line | Purpose |
|---|----------|------|---------|
| 23 | `metricTradeCloseRejectedQuoteStaleTotal` | L212 (approx) | Counter for stale-quote close rejections |
| 24 | `metricTradeTargetsRejectedQuoteStaleTotal` | L213 (approx) | Counter for stale-quote target update rejections |
| 25 | `metricWsQuotePermissionRefreshTotal` | L214 | Counter for WS quote permission refreshes |
| 26 | `metricWsQuotePermissionRefreshErrorsTotal` | L215 | Counter for quote permission refresh errors |
| 27 | `metricWsOriginRejectedTotal` | L216 | Counter for origin-rejected WS connections |
| 28 | `metricWsUserConnectionLimitRejectedTotal` | L217 | Counter for per-user connection limit rejections |
| 29 | `metricWsMessageRateLimitedTotal` | L218 | Counter for rate-limited WS messages |
| 30 | `queuedQuoteAnonRowId` | L5444 | Auto-incrementing ID for anonymous quote rows in batch |

> [!WARNING]
> The plan mentions "6 metric counters" in the WS Security table (L783) but **7 exist** (items 23–29). Items 23–24 are trade-specific metrics referenced in the metrics endpoint but defined alongside the WS metrics. They need to go in `wsContext.ts` (since the `/metrics` endpoint reads them all together) or a shared `server/lib/metricsState.ts`.

