## Category 10 — Already-Extracted Routers Not Fully Inventoried

The plan says "30 existing sub-files." There are exactly **30 files** in `server/routes/` but L5264–5296 registers **34 router mounts** (some files like `partnerPortal.ts` and `traderTalent.ts` register multiple mount points). The plan should list the exact registration order to prevent mount-order regressions during cleanup.

| Current Registration Order (L5264–5296) |
|---|
| 1. `registerAdminRoutes(app)` |
| 2. `registerMarketRoutes(app)` |
| 3. `registerMetaRoutes(app)` |
| 4. `registerMeSessionsRoutes(app)` |
| 5. `registerAdminSecurityRoutes(app)` |
| 6. `app.use("/api/i18n", i18nRouter)` |
| 7. `app.use("/api/instruments", instrumentsRouter)` |
| 8. `app.use(profileMfaRouter)` — no prefix! |
| 9. `app.use("/api/verification", verificationRouter)` |
| 10. `app.use("/api/legal", legalRouter)` |
| 11. `app.use("/api/admin/legal-docs-v2", adminLegalDocsRouter)` |
| 12. `app.use("/api/admin/legal-acceptances", adminLegalAcceptancesRouter)` |
| 13. `app.use("/api/admin/market-data", adminMarketDataRouter)` |
| 14. `app.use("/api/admin/quote-subscriptions", adminQuoteSubscriptionsRouter)` |
| 15. `app.use("/api/admin/system-config", adminSystemConfigRouter)` |
| 16. `app.use("/api/admin/activity", adminActivityRouter)` |
| 17. `app.use("/api/admin/i18n", adminI18nRouter)` |
| 18. `app.use("/api/quote-subscriptions", quoteSubscriptionsRouter)` |
| 19. `app.use("/api/mailbox", mailboxRouter)` |
| 20. `app.use("/api/notifications", notificationsRouter)` |
| 21. `app.use("/api/admin/scout", adminScoutRouter)` |
| 22. `app.use("/api/admin/challenges", adminChallengesRouter)` |
| 23. `app.use("/api/admin/partners", adminPartnersRouter)` |
| 24. `app.use("/api/partner", partnerAuthRouter)` |
| 25. `app.use("/api/partner", partnerPortalRouter)` |
| 26. `app.use("/api/trader", traderTalentPublicRouter)` |
| 27. `app.use("/api/trader", traderTalentRouter)` |
| 28. `registerGriftRoutes(app)` |
| 29. `app.use("/api/grift", griftPublicRouter)` |
| 30. `app.use("/api/admin/migration", adminMigrationRouter)` |
| 31. `app.use("/api/admin/legal-docs", adminLegalRouter)` — legacy |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Item 8** (`profileMfaRouter`) uses `app.use(profileMfaRouter)` with **no path prefix**. This means MFA routes are mounted at the app root — if the MFA router has routes like `/api/profile/mfa/...`, they work, but this is fragile. Worth verifying during decomposition.

